{{also|hegira}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Hejira]]
* [[Hijra]]
* [[Hijrah]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.}} {{term|Hejira|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|هجرة|tr=híjra||[[departure]], [[exodus]]|lang=ar}}, referring to Muhammad’s flight from [[Mecca]] to [[Medina]] in 622 {{C.E.}}; from the verb {{term|هجر|tr=hájara||to [[emigrate]], to [[abandon]]|lang=ar}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The [[emigration]] of [[Muhammad]] and his [[follower]]s from [[Mecca]] to [[Medina]] in 622 {{C.E.}} to escape persecution.
# The beginning of the [[Muslim]] [[era]], equivalent to July 16, 622, by the [[Julian calendar]] of the day.
#: ''Since the Muslim lunar year contains only 354 days, 2005 {{C.E.}} is approximately equivalent to Hegira 1426.''

